JOB SPECIFICATION
Senior Director, Revenue Operations &amp; Enablement
Reports To: Ed Mason, Chief Revenue Officer
Location: Raleigh, NC — In-Office (Prometheus Group HQ)
Level: Senior Director (VP path based on performance)
Team: Renewals, Business Development (BDR), Sales Enablement
Why This Role Exists
The CRO’s office needs an operational leader who owns the infrastructure that makes the sales team perform —
not by coaching individual deals, but by ensuring the engine that produces pipeline, protects revenue, and
develops sales talent runs at an inspectable standard across every region. This person owns three functions:
Renewals, BDR, and Sales Enablement.
This is a career-defining seat. You sit at the CRO’s right hand, learning how a global GTM organization operates
by cutting across departments and owning real outcomes. The VP title is available to the person who earns it by
making these three functions measurably better.
What You Own
Renewals
You own the renewal book: forecasting renewal revenue, inspecting execution across regions, enforcing pricing
discipline, and flagging at-risk accounts before they become escalations. Every renewal is a commercial
conversation, not an administrative one. No silent downsells, no multi-year rates on short-term extensions, no
concessions without commitments in return.
Business Development (BDR)
You own top-of-funnel pipeline generation. Hiring profiles, activity standards, lead-to-opportunity conversion
quality, and the handoff to AE/AM teams. You hold BDR managers accountable to pipeline targets, not activity
metrics. Pipeline that doesn’t convert is noise.
Sales Enablement
You own what the sales team knows and how fast new hires become productive. Onboarding, skills
development, content management, and product training. The critical difference: you measure whether
enablement changes behavior, not just whether it was delivered. Enablement that ships but doesn’t stick is the
same as enablement that doesn’t exist.
How You Operate
• Weekly cadence with the CRO: renewals forecast, BDR pipeline results, enablement impact. Data and
exceptions, not status updates.
• Cross-regional inspection. You have line of sight into every region and flag variance before it compounds.
• Direct accountability with Directors. If renewal execution or BDR conversion is below standard, you name
it and work the fix without waiting for the CRO to intervene.
• Build systems, not heroics. If a process breaks when you’re not watching, it’s not a system.

