What You Bring
Required
• 5+ years in B2B enterprise software: sales operations, revenue operations, or a commercial leadership
role.
• You have managed teams and been accountable for commercial outcomes, not just designed programs.
• Salesforce fluency — pipeline management, forecasting mechanics, CRM inspection. Reporting that drives
decisions, not decorates decks.
• Cross-regional operating experience. You know how to hold a standard across geographies
• The confidence to challenge senior sales leaders directly, with data, without drama.
• Hunger. You want to learn how a CRO runs a global commercial organization and you’re willing to earn
that education through operational work.
Preferred
• Industrial or asset-intensive software experience (oil and gas, utilities, mining, manufacturing).
• Comfort with AI tools. Prometheus is AI-forward — the CRO’s office uses AI for coaching, content creation,
and operational analysis.
• Experience building a function from scratch, not just optimizing an inherited one.
What This Role Is Not
This is not a deal coaching role. The CRO and Directors own deal strategy and customer-facing executive
engagement. You own the operational infrastructure that makes those activities productive. This is also not a
chief-of-staff or project management role — you own functions with direct reports, targets, and measurable
outcomes. The CRO’s right hand is an operator, not an organizer.
Compensation
Competitive base at Senior Director level for growth-stage enterprise software. Variable compensation tied to
renewal retention rate, BDR pipeline generation targets, and enablement adoption metrics. Equity participation.
